**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery Mission**

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|--------------|-------------------|
| G1 | Deliver requested resources to the requesting agent at the specified location | `;` | Perform | AND | The mission requires that all sub‑tasks (collection, delivery, failure handling, parallelism) be completed before the top‑level goal is satisfied. |
| G2 | Collection Phase | `;` | Perform | AND | All steps of the collection phase must be performed in the order defined by the mission. |
| G2.1 | Determine order of storage visits | `-` | Query | – | The robot must estimate waiting time and path length to decide the visiting order. |
| G2.2 | Request resource from storage | `-` | Perform | – | Sending a request message is an action that must be executed. |
| G2.3 | Wait for resource retrieval | `-` | Perform | – | The robot must wait until the storage confirms the resource has been retrieved. |
| G2.4 | Monitor battery level in collection phase | `-` | Query | – | Battery information is read, not produced. |
| G2.5 | Handle low battery (10 %) in collection phase | `-` | Perform | – | When battery falls below 10 % the robot must recharge and hand over the mission. |
| G3 | Delivery Phase | `;` | Perform | AND | All delivery steps must be performed sequentially (multiple runs). |
| G3.1 | Deliver resource to specified location | `-` | Perform | – | The robot must physically deliver the resource. |
| G3.2 | Monitor battery level in delivery phase | `-` | Query | – | Battery information is read during delivery. |
| G3.3 | Handle low battery (30 %) in delivery phase | `-` | Perform | – | When battery falls below 30 % the robot must return to a checkpoint and hand over the remaining task. |
| G4 | Failure handling | `#` | Perform | AND | Alert and report actions can be performed in parallel. |
| G4.1 | Trigger alert | `-` | Perform | – | The system must trigger an alert when the robot cannot return to a checkpoint. |
| G4.2 | Send report to sector manager | `-` | Perform | – | The sector manager must receive a failure report. |
| G5 | Parallel collect‑deliver tasks for multiple items | `#` | Perform | AND | Assigning robots for collection and delivery can be done in parallel to reduce mission time. |
| G5.1 | Assign robots to collection tasks | `-` | Perform | – | Multiple robots may be needed to collect from different storages. |
| G5.2 | Assign robots to delivery tasks | `-` | Perform | – | Multiple robots may be needed to deliver to different destinations. |

---

### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|-----------------------|-------------------|
| AT1 | Estimate waiting time at the storage | AND | storage | 1 | Only the collecting robot needs to estimate waiting time. |
| AT2 | Compute path length to the storage | AND | robot navigation | 1 | Single robot computes its own path. |
| AT3 | Combine estimates to determine visiting order | AND | robot | 1 | One robot decides the order. |
| AT4 | Send request message to storage | AND | storage | 1 | Only the collecting robot sends the request. |
| AT5 | Wait for confirmation from storage | AND | storage | 1 | The same robot waits for the reply. |
| AT6 | Read battery level (collection) | AND | robot | 1 | Robot monitors its own battery. |
| AT7 | Go to recharging station | AND | recharging station | 1 | Robot must recharge when battery <10 %. |
| AT8 | Assign mission to another robot | AND | control center | 1 | Only one assignment action is needed. |
| AT9 | Move resource to destination | AND | destination | 1 | Robot delivers the resource. |
| AT10 | Confirm delivery | AND | destination | 1 | Robot confirms that the resource has arrived. |
| AT11 | Read battery level (delivery) | AND | robot | 1 | Robot monitors its own battery during delivery. |
| AT12 | Return resource to checkpoint | AND | checkpoint | 1 | Robot must return when battery <30 %. |
| AT13 | Assign remaining task to another robot | AND | control center | 1 | Only one assignment action is needed. |
| AT14 | Trigger alert | AND | alert system | 1 | System triggers an alert on failure. |
| AT15 | Send report to sector manager | AND | sector manager | 1 | Robot sends a failure report. |
| AT16 | Assign robots for collection | AND | control center | [1,n] | Multiple robots may be required for parallel collection. |
| AT17 | Assign robots for delivery | AND | control center | [1,n] | Multiple robots may be required for parallel delivery. |

